1
00:04:56,666 --> 00:05:02,666
Twelve chances to get it right.

2
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:59,333
12 Dates of Christmas is a romance, comedy,
fantasy film directed by James Hayman.

3
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:56,000
In an attempt to win back her ex-boyfriend Jack on Christmas Eve, Kate ends up
ruining her blind date with Miles, a handsome guy she's been set up with.

4
00:19:46,666 --> 00:19:52,666
In a strange twist of fate, Kate is magically given the
chance to re-live Christmas Eve twelve times!

5
00:24:43,333 --> 00:24:49,333
Kate Stanton, played by Amy Smart.

6
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Miles Dufine, played by Mark-Paul Gosselaar.

7
00:34:36,666 --> 00:34:42,666
Jack Evans, played by Benjamin Ayres.

8
00:39:33,333 --> 00:39:39,333
Mike Stanton, played by Peter MacNeill.

9
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Sally Stanton, played by Mary Long.

10
00:49:26,666 --> 00:49:32,666
Margine Frumkin, played by Jayne Eastwood.

11
00:54:23,333 --> 00:54:29,333
12 Dates of Christmas is a television film starring
Amy Smart and Mark-Paul Gosselaar.

12
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
It premiered on ABC Family on December 11, 2011 in their
25 Days of Christmas programming block.

13
01:04:16,666 --> 01:04:22,666
It is directed by James Hayman.

14
01:09:13,333 --> 01:09:19,333
The film depicts Smart as Kate, a woman insensitive to the feelings of others and who wants to return to a
past relationship, and Gosselaar as Miles, a widower who hopes to find a new romantic partner.

15
01:14:10,000 --> 01:14:16,000
After Kate blows off her blind date with Miles on Christmas Eve, she discovers she is stuck in a time-loop,
giving her 12 chances to mature, improve her relationships with others, and find romance with Miles.

16
01:19:06,666 --> 01:19:12,666
The film explores themes of new york city, christmas
party, blind date, time loop, falling in love.

17
01:24:03,333 --> 01:24:09,333
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and mind_bending.
